### Cross-Cutting Details

**Promotion**  
Technical excellence is required but not sufficient. Each step upward also tests whether the candidate will stop asking certain classes of question. Those who cannot make that adjustment remain (or are kept) at their current level.

**Knowledge Policing**  
Mostly social and structural rather than violent. Curiosity is redirected. Over-curious workers are given heavier ordinary workloads or quietly passed over. Actual disappearances are rare and reserved for clear, repeated threats to the system.

**Internal Language**  
Lower ranks talk about “heavy air,” “purple work,” and “sensitive runs.”  
Line Keepers speak of “load” and “balance.”  
Threadwrights speak of “the weave” and, in private, “the cost.”

**Loyalty**  
The guild’s deepest loyalty is to continuity. Even Threadwrights who hate the extraction will usually still repair a failing section, because the alternative is immediate civic harm to people who had no say in the arrangement.

